I say that {C} the third is also square.

Since between {A} and {C} there is one mean proportional number, {B}, therefore {A} and {C} are similar plane numbers. But {A} is square, therefore {C} is also square. [!just VIII.20]

Therefore, *if three numbers are in continued proportion, and the first is square, then the third is also square.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
